n states \"Édition 2012\" hmm. The title page of R 137-1:2012 says \"OIML R 137-1 Edition 2012 (E)\". So Edition 2012. I'll use 2012.\n\nAccuracy class: 1.0. accuracy_classes: [1.0] or [\"1.0\"]? Schema doesn't specify type. I'll use [\"1.0\"] as string... or number 1.0. Certificate says \"1.0\". I'll use \"1.0\" as string to preserve the display form. Hmm, actually numbers might be better: [1.0]. But \"1.0\" as a float would render 1.0. I'll use [\"1.0\"].\n\n**Test reports:**\n- No. NMi-12200520-02 dated 22 September 2014, 39 pages — role: type_evaluation_report\n- No. NMi-2514194-02 dated 5 January 2021, 10 pages — role: test_report (or evaluation report). The first one \"includes\" the Type Evaluation Report per page 1 (\"represented by the sample(s) identified in the OIML Type Evaluation Report\"). I'll mark first as type_evaluation_report, second as test_report.\n\n**Revision history:**\n- Initial, 28 September 2021, changes \"-\" (initial issue) → changes: \"Initial issue\" or omit? The table says description \"-\". I'll say \"Initial issue\".\n- 1, 1 May 2025, \"Correction of the lubrication oil density in Table 1\"\n\n**Characteristics Table 1 (type_level):**\n- destined_for_measurement_of: \"Gas volume\" (string value)\n- environmental_class: \"M1\"\n- accuracy_class: \"1.0\"\n- maximum_pressure: \"See tables 2 and 4\" — it's a reference, not a value. Could record as string value \"See tables 2 and 4\". Per rules, formulas/symbols as strings. This is a text reference; I'll include with string value or omit. I'll include as string value \"See tables 2 and 4\". Hmm, rule 8 says don't fabricate; including the reference as a string is faithful. I'll include it.\n- ambient_temperature_range: {min: -10, max: 55}, unit °C\n- gas_temperature_range: {min: -10, max: 55}, unit °C\n- designed_for: \"Condensing humidity\"\n- orientation: \"Horizontal / vertical up / vertical down / All orientations\" → \"All orientations\" — I'll put \"All orientations (horizontal / ve