(83 vs 103), different characteristics. So model_id should include diameter: \"DN80-G100\" etc. Or \"G100-80\". I'll use model_id like \"DN80/G100\", \"DN100/G160\". And in model_level attributes, model references those ids.\n\nLet me construct the full list of 19 models with their characteristics:\n\nTable 2 (measuring part) — expand rowspans:\n| DN | G | Impeller dia | Blade height | Vane thickness | Blade angle | # blades |\n- 50, 65, 51, 5, 15.5, 45, 12\n- 80, 100, 83, 12, 22, 45, 14\n- 80, 160, 83, 12, 22, 45, 14\n- 80, 250, 83, 12, 22, 45, 14\n- 100, 160, 103, 15, 28, 45, 14\n- 100, 250, 103, 15, 28, 45, 14\n- 100, 400, 103, 15, 28, 45, 14\n- 150, 400, 154, 22, 27, 45, 16\n- 150, 650, 154, 22, 27, 45, 16\n- 150, 1000, 154, 22, 27, 45, 16\n- 200, 650, 198, 40, 27, 45, 18\n- 200, 1000, 198, 40, 27, 45, 18\n- 200, 1600, 198, 40, 27, 45, 18\n- 250, 1000, 246, 32, 30, 45, 20\n- 250, 1600, 246, 32, 30, 45, 20\n- 250, 2500, 246, 32, 30, 45, 20\n- 300, 1600, 296, 35.5, 30, 45, 22\n- 300, 2500, 296, 35.5, 30, 45, 22\n- 300, 4000, 296, 35.5, 30, 45, 22\n\nNote: \"Vane thickness\" column — values 15,5 / 22 / 28 / 27 / 27 / 30 / 30. Wait, header: Impeller diameter, Blade height, Vane thickness, Blade angle, Number of blades. Row 50: 51, 5, 15,5, 45, 12 → impeller 51, blade height 5, vane thickness 15.5, blade angle 45, blades 12. Hmm, vane thickness 15.5 mm seems large but that's what's written. Actually for G65 the impeller is 51mm... blade height 5, vane thickness 15,5 — hmm could be; not my problem. For DN80: 83, 12, 22, 45, 14 → impeller 83, blade height 12, vane thickness 22, angle 45, blades 14. OK.\n\nTable 3 (bearings) — diameter rows with main shaft inlet/outlet, Cr inlet/outlet, C0r inlet/outlet (Static load rating \"C_or\" — subscript \"or\" means C0r), and max operating pressure column for 16 bar(g) and 100 bar(g):\n- 50: shaft 2/2, Cr 286/286, C0r 90/90 → 16 bar: \"permanently lubricated bearings, double shielded\"\n- 80: 3/3, 644/644, 215/215 → 16 bar: same\