0, 1600, 320, 80, -, 53,3, -] = 7 items:\n1. G = 1000\n2. Qmax = 1600\n3. Qt = 320\n4. MR1:20@0-100 = 80?? \n\nHmm no. 1600/20 = 80. So col4 = 80 would be Qmin for MR1:20@0-100 = 80. Then col5 = -, col6 = 53.3 (1600/30 = 53.33 ✓), col7 = -.\n\nWait but that contradicts my earlier reading. Let me recount the cells: \"1000\", \"1600\", \"320\", \"80\", \"-\", \"53,3\", \"-\" — yes that's 7 cells. So:\n- G=1000, Qmax=1600, Qt=320 (1600/5=320 ✓)\n- MR1:20@0-100bar = 80 (1600/20 = 80 ✓)\n- MR1:20@8-100bar = -\n- MR1:30@8-100bar = 53.3 (1600/30 ≈ 53.33 ✓)\n- MR1:30@16-100bar = -\n\nHmm OK so I misread earlier. Let me redo ALL rows carefully by counting cells. Each data row should have 7 cells (DN comes from rowspan where applicable).\n\nRow A: `<tr><td>50</td><td>65</td><td>100</td><td>20</td><td>5</td><td>-</td><td>3,3</td><td>-</td></tr>` — 8 cells (includes DN): DN=50, G=65, Qmax=100, Qt=20, c5=5, c6=-, c7=3.3, c8=-. So MR1:20@0-100=5, MR1:20@8-100=-, MR1:30@8-100=3.3, MR1:30@16-100=-.\n\nRow B (DN80 rowspan): `<tr><td>100</td><td>160</td><td>32</td><td>-</td><td>8</td><td>-</td><td>5,3</td></tr>` — 7 cells: G=100, Qmax=160, Qt=32, c4=-, c5=8, c6=-, c7=5.3. So MR1:20@0-100=-, MR1:20@8-100=8, MR1:30@8-100=-, MR1:30@16-100=5.3.\n\nRow C: `<tr><td>160</td><td>250</td><td>50</td><td>12,5</td><td>-</td><td>8,3</td><td>-</td></tr>` — G=160, Qmax=250, Qt=50, MR1:20@0-100=12.5, MR1:20@8-100=-, MR1:30@8-100=8.3, MR1:30@16-100=-.\n\nRow D: `<tr><td>250</td><td>400</td><td>80</td><td>20</td><td>-</td><td>13,3</td><td>-</td></tr>` — G=250, Qmax=400, Qt=80, MR1:20@0-100=20, MR1:20@8-100=-, MR1:30@8-100=13.3, MR1:30@16-100=-.\n\nRow E (DN100): `<tr><td>160</td><td>250</td><td>50</td><td>-</td><td>12,5</td><td>-</td><td>8,3</td></tr>` — G=160, Qmax=250, Qt=50, MR1:20@0-100=-, MR1:20@8-100=12.5, MR1:30@8-100=-, MR1:30@16-100=8.3.\n\nRow F: `<tr><td>250</td><td>400</td><td>80</td><td>20</td><td>-</td><td>13,3</td><td>-</td></tr>` — G=250: MR1:20@0-100=20, MR1:30@8-100=13.3.\n\nRow G: `