50, M12 DN200-G1000, M13 DN200-G1600, M14 DN250-G1000, M15 DN250-G1600, M17 DN300-G1600 → 15 models with 0.02); M16 DN250-G2500, M18 DN300-G2500, M19 DN300-G4000 → 0.2. Total 1+15+3=19 ✓.\n\nNow config_level:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"maximum_operating_pressure\",\n    \"axis\": \"bearing_lubrication_type\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"condition\": \"Permanently lubricated, double shielded bearings (DN 50, 80, 100)\", \"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar(g)\", \"footnote_markers\": []},\n      {\"condition\": \"External oil pump lubricated, single or double shielded bearings (DN 150, 200, 250, 300)\", \"value\": 100, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar(g)\", \"footnote_markers\": []}\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"prescribed_inlet_pipe_length\",\n    \"axis\": \"flow_disturbance\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"condition\": \"Severe flow disturbances\", \"value\": 2, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\", \"footnote_markers\": []},\n      {\"condition\": \"Mild flow disturbances\", \"value\": null, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n    ]\n  }\n]\n```\n\nHmm wait, in Table 3: DN50/80/100 have \"permanently lubricated, double shielded\" under 16 bar(g) and also appear under the 100 bar(g) column with \"external oil pump lubricated\" (that column spans all 7 rows). So DN50–100 could be either: permanently lubricated limited to 16 bar, or external pump lubricated for up to 100 bar. DN150–300: only external pump lubricated (16 bar column is \"-\"). So my config conditions: condition 1 \"permanently lubricated, double shielded bearings (DN 50–100): max 16 bar(g)\"; condition 2 \"external oil pump lubricated, single or double shielded bearings (all diameters DN 50–300): max 100 bar(g)\". Let me phrase: values: [{condition: \"Permanently lubricated, double shielded bearings (DN 50–100)\", value 16}, {condition: \"External oil pump lubricated, single or double shielded bearings (DN 50–300)\", value 100}]. Good.\n\nmatrix_tables:\n\nTable 2:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Table 2 – General characteristics of the family of instruments: Measuring part\",\n  \"columns\": [\"diameter\", \"g_value\", \"impeller_diameter\", \"blade_height\", \"vane_thickness\", \"blade_angle\", \"number_of_blades\"],\n  \"column_units\": [\"mm\", null, \"mm\", \"mm\", \"mm\", \"°\", null],\n  \"rows\": [19 rows],\n  \"description\": null,\n  \"footnotes\": []\n}\n```\n\nWait — schema for matrix_tables: {name, columns[], rows[] (object per row), description, footnotes[]}. The R137 example added column_units — the example in the prompt includes \"column_units\". I'll include it too (the prompt's example schema for matrix_tables in rule 4 includes column_units). Good.\n\nTable 3:\ncolumns: [\"diameter\", \"main_shaft_diameter_inlet\", \"main_shaft_diameter_outlet\", \"dynamic_load_rating_cr_inlet\", \"dynamic_load_rating_cr_outlet\", \"static_load_rating_c0r_inlet\", \"static_load_rating_c0r_outlet\", \"max_operating_pressure_bearing_type_16_bar_g\", \"max_operating_pressure_bearing_type_100_bar_g\"]\nHmm, simpler: \"bearing_type_at_16_bar_g\", \"bearing_type_at_100_bar_g\".\ncolumn_units: [\"mm\",\"mm\",\"mm\",\"N\",\"N\",\"N\",\"N\",null,null]\nrows 7 with strings/null.\n\nTable 4:\ncolumns: [\"diameter\",\"g_value\",\"qmax\",\"qt\",\"qmin_mr_1_20_0_100_bar_g\",\"qmin_mr_1_20_8_100_bar_g\",\"qmin_mr_1_30_8_100_bar_g\",\"qmin_mr_1_30_16_100_bar_g\"]\ncolumn_units: [\"mm\", null, \"m³/h\",\"m³/h\",\"m³/h\",\"m³/h\",\"m³/h\",\"m³/h\"]\ndescription: \"Minimum Qmin values for the specified pressure range. '-' (null) = not applicable. MR = measuring range (Qmax/Qmin = 1:20 or 1:30). Permanently lubricated bearings limit the maximum operating pressure to 16 bar(g) (see Table 3).\"\nfootnotes: []\n\nTable 5:\ncolumns: [\"type\",\"number_of_drums_before_comma\",\"number_of_drums_behind_comma\",\"control_element\"]\ncolumn_units: [null,null,null,\"m³\"]\nrows:\n{\"type\":\"G65\",\"number_of_drums_before_comma\":6,\"number_of_drums_behind_comma\":2,\"control_element\":0.002}\n{\"type\":\"G100 – G1600\",7,1,0.02}\n{\"type\":\"G2000 – G4000\",8,0,0.2}\n\nNow write everything. Also check: \"Impeller diameter\" for DN300 is 296, blade height 35,5 → 35.5. Yes: `<td>296</td><td>35,5</td><td>30</td><td>45</td><td>22</td>`. Good.\n\nAlso project_number: \"3939314\" — string or number? It's an identifier; keep as string.\n\naccuracy_classes: [\"1.0\"] — the class 1.0 for gas meters. Keep string.\n\nOne more: certificate scheme \"A\" — \"This OIML Certificate is issued under scheme A.\" ✓\n\nrecommendation.amendment: not mentioned → omit or null. I'll omit.\n\ntest_reports roles: first — \"that includes\" the Type Evaluation Report? Page 1 says \"represented by the sample(s) identified in the OIML Type Evaluation Report\". The report NMi-12200520-02 dated 2014 is presumably the type evaluation report; NMi-2514194-02 (2021) is likely a follow-up/surveillance test report (for the 2021 initial certificate). Roles: \"type_evaluation_report\" and \"test_report\". OK.\n\nLet me now also double check Table 3 rows for DN100: `<tr><td>100</td><td>4</td><td>4</td><td>1339</td><td>644</td><td>488</td><td>215</td></tr>` → Cr inlet 1339, outlet 644; C0r inlet 488, outlet 215. ✓ matches my arrays.\n\nDN150: Cr 1646/1339, C0r 663/488 ✓.\n\nNow assemble the final JSON. It'll be long; that's fine. No markdown fences, no commentary.\n\nOne consideration: should \"maximum_pressure\" type_level be included as string reference? I'll include with value \"See tables 2 and 4\". Fine.\n\nAlso add \"inlet_pipe_length\" note? Covered by config_level.\n\nAlso \"positions\": orientation covers it.\n\nWriting model_level values arrays with model ids — long but necessary.\n\nLet me write the JSON now carefully.\n\nAlso decide label format: \"TBQM G65 (DN 50)\".\n\nFinal check on decimals: 15,5→15.5; 35,5→35.5; 2,5→2.5; 58,48→58.48; 3,3→3.3; 5,3→5.3; 8,3→8.3; 12,5→12.5; 13,3→13.3; 21,7→21.7; 33,3→33.3; 53,3→53.3; 83,3→83.3; 133,3→133.3; 216,7→216.7; 0,002→0.002.\